 to=self<|message|>You are a writer in the UK, writing books for UK children.

Write short story <200 words to describe the rainbows that you like the most.

Make sure UK English. Use simple words.

Write short story <200 words.

Let's produce ~150 words.<|start|>assistant to=user<|message|>I like the rainbows that come after rain in summer.

They are not big and bright. They are small and soft, like a watercolour wash in the sky.

I saw one last week over the park. The sun was low and warm. The grass was wet and shiny. A thin rainbow stood over the swings.

It was pink and lilac and a little bit green. It did not touch the ground. It just floated there, quiet.

Mum said, “Look, love.” I said, “It’s a shy rainbow.”

I like shy rainbows best. They don’t shout. They just sit there for a minute, then fade away.

If you are quick, you can wave at them. I think they wave back. [end of text]


